s steps and unit plane normal. Basis steps are measured native-to-WCS mappings, not assumed unit axes. The requested stored sketch geometry is read completely where supported; unsupported types are explicit and actual byte limits still apply. Polyline segment indices describe geometry order, not constraint subentity identities. Omit for metadata only. Geometry does not evaluate constraints or prove solver status. Optional sketch_ids reads exact same-owner native sketch geometry, retained source bindings, peer profiles, observed constraint scope and a fresh sketch_token, including document construction outside body composition. Optional include_document_sketches discovers native sketch identity pages; document_sketch_cursor continues under the same revision. These fields are omitted by default and never enter edit mode or solve constraints. Optional include_document_profiles reads profile identity pages in the selected parts' actual native owner document, including unused document construction. Its ID may differ from ordinary history's DWG container; selected bodies must share one actual owner scope; use document_profile_cursor from the preceding page under the same revision. Optional profile_ids selects exact native profiles for document_profiles with actual parent, native hosts, support, oriented plane, selected contour, retained source projections and fresh once-consumption token. These IDs are not body membership claims or DWG handles. Ordinary history performs no document construction scan. Optional profile_element_ids reads actual Line/Arc/Circle element identities, source links, full native selected boundaries/constraint observation and a fresh element_token for unused actual-owner construction or consumed profiles of one target part. It is omitted by default. Optional profile_region_ids reads exact consumed Circle profiles of one selected part, returning actual selected native area/hole loops, element/source identities and a fresh region_token; this is separate from unused profile_ids metadata. It does not enter edit mode or evaluate the internal MCS solver. Optional extrusion_extent_ids reads exact existing extrusions of one selected part with actual native modes, first/second lengths and tapers, owning driver state, retained profile/parent, current extent_token and complete-body WCS bounds. The actual owner document may differ from the active DWG lookup container. Omitted by default; this read does not enter edit mode or solve constraints. Native sketch constraint enumeration may be unavailable: constraint_observations/constraint_observation then report constraints_complete=false and constraints=null with a warning. This never means an empty network or verified preservation of unobservable constraints. Actual manager/owner/sketch scope and observed geometry/source/feature/driver checks remain, while available inventories are fully compared. These observation and feature-specific editors do not set sketch constraints; internal relation/control writes use their owning operation schemas. Optional include_document_datum_planes discovers readonly WorkPlane identity pages in the selected parts' one shared actual native owner document; continue document_datum_cursor under the same revision. Optional datum_plane_ids reads exact physical planes, native definition/source/driver/consumer IDs, actual host/body membership and fresh datum_token. Optional datum_plane_revision_ids reads a retained fixed non-GCS plane already consumed by exact native Mirrors with healthy material source features in the selected current part and actual owner document, returning direct mirror/source/subfeature IDs and a fresh whole revision_token beside datum_token. Omitted by default; no setter, solver or view refresh occurs in this read. These fields are omitted by default; no document scan, plane creation, solver or rebuild occurs in ordinary history.",
