1 Spline (open or closed) by checking every actual segment pair, solver=analytic_finite_segments, coordinates within +/-1e9 and exact WCSXY/Z0. Positive weights reparameterize these straight segments; no curved spline is approximated. A full native Circle in WCSXY/Z0 with radius<=1e9 is also supported against closed degree1 Spline by analytic segment-circle minima, solver=analytic_segment_circle. This is distance between the curves, so nested boundaries can have a positive gap. A finite native Arc in WCSXY/Z0 with radius<=1e9 is supported by endpoint, intersection and interior stationary-pair enumeration, solver=analytic_segment_arc; its actual signed sweep is respected. Ellipse, smooth Spline and other closed-spline operands remain excluded. Point-to-curve nearest in metrics is unchanged. intersections: two finite curves, complete isolated points within actual response bytes; overlap is not evaluated in this mode. distance: two finite curves, minimum Euclidean distance and an ordered closest pair which may be nonunique. relations: two curves in WCS XY/Z=0 only, intersection points and positive-length common intervals; complete witnesses within actual response bytes. Complete curve geometry is bounded by actual serialized bytes and cancellation. containment: one Circle or simple closed straight Polyline with at least three vertices and one WCS XY/Z0 point, classified inside/outside/boundary by conservative exclusion against native extents followed by a temporary native Region BRep face. The extents exclusion leaves a margin max(1e-6, max_abs_extent*1e-12) drawing units; within that band the BRep result or explicit inconsistency error is preserved. No holes, self-intersections, bulges or nonplanar contours. No curve extension/projection. Native kernel tolerance, drawing units and squared units for area;Read-only metrics may return complete=false and remaining_handles when the diagnostic time budget is reached after useful results; continue with those handles. No document changes." + " " + SolidMeasurementSchema409.Description,
