 or unresolved/foreign ownership need their owning route. This does not copy a viewport, transfer a layout, edit Model geometry or make annotation followers. Opaque native/field internals are unobserved. Recovery/Undo is uncertain; unknown is not success. Plan the visible detail and boundary against existing sheet annotations, then inspect one rendered group image and relevant readback. set_viewport_view edits supported existing camera/on/layer-freezing fields with committed readback; read current metadata first. copy_viewport/delete_viewport use existing ordinary rectangular native Paper viewport handles and explicit active layout_handle. Copy preserves the retained model camera, frame size/scale, frozen layers, locked state and appearance; center locates the new frame, optional is_on controls the copy. Native provenance is returned in viewport_lifecycle_results. Delete leaves model geometry and other sheet entities intact. The native overview viewport1 and linked/clipped/perspective views need their owning route. New viewport creation is available without guaranteed rollback/Undo; it returns ROLLBACK_NOT_GUARANTEED. Readback is checked after Commit/disposal. Create_drawing_views adds a group from a top-level direct Solid3d or native Mc3dSolid: one root with optional Top/selected projections, explicit scale and XY placement, optional WCS projection basis; existing healthy Model Space views are preserved. Optional layout_handle together with target_space paper creates fresh linked native views in that exact active ordinary Paper sheet (CVPORT1). Sources remain explicit top-level Model solids, placement is sheet XY; actual native sheet/source/tree and projection observations are returned. Refresh get_drawing_views tokens and inspect rendered detail. This creates native projected views independently from rectangular viewports; it does not move a retained group between layouts or attach annotation followers. Read the projection plane, not just the native direction label. Create_section_view adds a planar native Section and root view when its complete native Model solid composition is the intended detail. source_handles declares that composition. Selected subsets with other visible Model solids on on/thawed layers are not retained by this native path and return SECTION_SOURCE_SELECTION_UNSUPPORTED before object changes. Hidden/off/frozen state alone is not proof of a narrower retained source set; actual complete native view participants must establish any such scope. Fresh native generation settings record the requested sources, but stored settings or sliced intersections do not prove projection selection. Exact complete view participation is checked separately from configuration-derived Section processing. Existing settings/destinations/appearance and model sources remain checked. Optionally specify viewing/vertical WCS directions together. set_section_view_cut changes the two WCS cut-line vertices of a retained ordinary non-live Plane Section in its existing viewing/vertical basis. Read get_drawing_views section_cut and provide its section token plus all associated views/descendants and their current layout/view tokens. The same native Section/views, explicit Model sources, placed projection/view planes, scales, tree and model bodies remain. It regenerates the group without recreating objects; live, support-driven, jogged/notched cuts and layout transfer require their owning routes. Native rollback/Undo is not guaranteed. set_drawing_view_sources changes an explicit complete ordinary root/descendant group using fresh view tokens; rename_drawing_view preserves identity; add_drawing_view_child creates a genuine linked native projection. Read current sources/tree and plan placement before mutation. No parameter updates. Create ordinary layers or text styles, change layer ACI/RGB, explicit transparency, description and supported visibility/line properties, replace insertion attribute text, define static 2D blocks or insert existing 