ns. " +
                "Modify existing direct Solid3d with transform_solid (WCS XYZ translation, arbitrary-axis rotation, mirror, positive uniform scale), erase or set_properties; direct bodies keep their handles. For an appended native join/cut from an explicit contour, add_model_extrusion creates owned native sketch inputs. Use create_model_sketch, create_model_profile_on_sketch and add_model_extrusion_from_profile when constraints, actual support or reuse express the required design intent; use fresh native IDs and tokens. Initial model_extrusion and retained-source variants keep their separate scopes. Native history edits have no guaranteed rollback. Read exact geometry and refresh topology after changes. set_polyline_geometry inserts/removes/replaces vertices and opens/closes an independent Polyline in place; set_polyline_corners applies selected fillets/chamfers, reverse_polyline preserves the physical contour while reversing traversal. All three use full expected_geometry including segment widths and curvature, preserve the entity handle, and require independent source ownership. set_polyline_vertices moves selected contour vertices using expected positions, preserving vertex count, closure and widths; paired expected_bulge/bulge edits outgoing curvature on independent profiles. set_curve_geometry updates Line endpoints, Circle center/radius or independent Arc center/radius/start/sweep in radians using explicit expected geometry; these are direct edits, not parametric constraints. Optional workplane on set_curve_geometry edits independent Line/Circle/Arc/Ellipse/Spline using frame-local coordinates/controls while retaining the native root and stored properties. Arc/Ellipse frame normals match the source; Spline keeps the established complete clamped NURBS grammar. Omission preserves existing XY behavior. Read WCS geometry and use the same explicit frame for expectations and replacements. trim_curve removes a picked interval using finite boundaries, extend_curve extends an endpoint to the nearest boundary, and offset_curve creates a parallel/concentric contour. Its explicit native_positive/native_negative modes call the native kernel once for zero-thickness Line/Arc/Circle or planar open/concave/bulged Polyline/Ellipse/Spline in Model/active ordinary Paper, including tilted planes. Optional workplane passes its oriented normal to the native factory without projection and is required for a Line with no unique offset plane; source and all generated independent roots are retained. Native sign is orientation/family dependent; complete native Spline detail is read-only; legacy create/replace/transform scopes remain separate. Native trim_curve/split_curve/extend_curve mode uses the current geometry.native_curve.curve_token and actual native parameters for Line/Arc/Circle/planar Polyline/Ellipse/Spline in actual WCS. Optional workplane imposes coplanarity without projection; a Line otherwise uses its actual finite WCS locus and collinear extension. Closed curves have no extendable endpoints. Read the selected schema and actual returned provenance. Read per-operation source/type bounds. Contour outputs are independent geometry with source-to-result provenance in contour_results; copied handles remain in copies only for ordinary copy. Legacy move/rotate/scale/copy/erase or layer/ACI color/linetype/lineweight edits support native Line/Circle/Arc/Ellipse/clamped Spline/Polyline/Text/MText and direct Solid3d in active Model Space; legacy transforms retain XY/Z-axis semantics. Ellipse requires WCSXY/Z0 normal+Z and bounded native extents. Spline requires degree1-5, complete finite controls, no fit data and every controlZ exactly0. Open splines must be nonperiodic; closed splines require clamped knots and exactly repeated first/last controls, no fields or persistent dependencies. Native periodic reporting is preserved. Closed spline block members require an attribute-free definition; the same bounded clamped XY spline geometry guards apply. Paired analysis supports only intersections/relations in the analyze_geometry scope. Existing exact native non-annotative static BlockReference supports native move/rotate/positive uniform scale/copy in requested active Model or ordinary Paper (CVPORT1), preserving shared definitions and owned variable single-line attributes. Existing placement can traverse static local nested inserts and native planar Line/Circle/Arc/Ellipse/Spline/Polyline/DBText/MText/single-line attribute leaves. Native local symbols and horizontal non-shape text styles are required; no INSERT layer-0, fixed-height or definition-units whitelist is imposed on existing placement. XY/Z0/+Z and positive uniform scale remain required. Root attributes support left/center/right and defined vertical alignment, invisible labels, positive width and finite oblique; active native alignment anchors transform with the occurrence. No fields, reactors, annotative contexts, fit/aligned/multiline attributes, dynamic/anonymous/xref/dependent/custom graphs or cycles. complete graph snapshots use actual bytes and cancellation. Other occurrences and definition member identities/data remain unchanged. Copy returns native root provenance, preserves source and same shared definition/space; copy-only per source in its group, with root/attribute extension dictionaries and XData excluded. Basic root erase/set_properties do not require definition traversal and preserve unselected shared definitions/occurrences; appearance supports layer/ACI/linetype/lineweight/linetype_scale/visible and unspecified stored properties remain. Attribute transforms/copies disclose uncertain Undo/rollback; unknown is not success. New INSERT/DEFINE retain the separate flat layer-0 Millimeters template scope described by modify_structure, with complete request, source and result byte admission. Ordinary curve edits/transforms and native offset/finishing routes observe complete source geometry with serialized-byte budgets and cancellation; legacy Spline mutation retains its separately stated native-family admission. No projection or nonuniform transform. set_curve_geometry also replaces independent Ellipse axes/ratio/parametric span and Spline full clamped NURBS controls/degree/knots/weights/closure, retaining the entity handle and properties; complete expected_geometry required. No fit/unclamped periodic sources; see operation schema.  replace_mleader_text replaces a single-line literal in one native straight non-annotative MText-content MLeader with one enabled horizontal landing, preserving its native text connection, style and vertices; the text insertion point may reflow around that fixed connection. No fields, formatting or columns; do not combine content and placement edits of the same leader in one request. Text1..4096 and expected_text0..16384; the complete batch is admitted by actual bytes. replace_text replaces literal content of exactly one ordinary native single-line Text per operation while retaining its justification, meaningful anchors and font/frame; native Align/Fit may adjust derived glyph sizing. expected_text must match the current value after preceding edits. No MText, attributes, fields or CAD percent codes. Replacement1..4096 characters. replace_mtext replaces visible literal paragraphs of one ordinary native MText with any retained attachment and background, preserving placement, width, text height, style, direction, line spacing and one uniform formatting envelope. expected_paragraphs must match after preceding edits; mixed formatting runs, fields, stacked fractions, columns and annotative contexts need their owning adapter. Each side has a nonempty paragraph array, each at most2048 characters, total4096 plain/8192 encoded; replacement must contain visible text. set_hatch_properties edits the stored native properties of one exact Hatch in Model or active ordinary Paper. Read geometry.editing.hatch_token from inspect_objects; optionally select SOLID or an installed predefined pattern, change radians angle, positive scale, OCS origin, island style and double pattern. Without pattern_name retain the existing predefined/UserDefined/custom pattern; positive pattern_space edits retained UserDefined spacing. Native loops, plane and local associative boundary references stay attached; no contour reconstruction, detached PAT availability test or estimated hatch-line count gate. Distinct hatches may share a request, but their roots and associative boundaries cannot have other mutations in that request. Gradient/foreign/unclassified dependency content needs its owning route. No guaranteed rollback/Undo; unknown is not success. Legacy set_hatch_pattern remains narrow ANSI31 compatibility; prefer set_hatch_properties. set_hatch_boundary supplies a complete polygon/circle outline and disjoint strictly interior polygon/circle holes for an existing independent Hatch, with its fresh hatch_token and retained OCS plane, identity, pattern and ordinary owned data. Empty holes removes holes; no source reconstruction or automatic association. Read geometry.editing.boundary_replacement and the exact specialized schema. Recovery and Undo are not guaranteed. set_dimension_line changes the line offset of one native aligned/rotated dimension, preserving measured endpoints/value/style/text. expected_dimline_point and dimline_point are WCSXY pairs; old points on the same physical line are equivalent. Coordinates +/-1e6mm, automatic text layout only, no fields/persistent dependencies, complete batch admitted by actual bytes. Native layout may slide the stored point along the requested line. replace_table_text edits a nonempty set of unique cells of one native Table per operation, with exact expected_text and unchanged observed formatting/geometry. Only plain unmerged string cells, no fields, formulas, links or formatting codes; the whole table must meet this scope and fit the actual serialized observation budget. resize_table sets sparse row heights and column widths (zero-based index, expected_size, size in millimeters), retaining ordinary native String/Long/Double slots including empty/multiple-content cells, raw value/type/unit/bits/order/data format, native Flow/stacking, style/appearance/overrides, owned metadata, placement and other sizes. Fields/blocks/formulas/links remain outside sizing. Indexed Tables require a resize-only request; automatic unoverridden scalar scale may reflow, with explicit scale/auto mode retained. Both rows and columns arrays required, at least one size edit; each size0.001..1000000. No persistent dependencies or locked formatting; native clamping fails. Ordered combination with replace_table_text allowed. Independent native Table placement/copy uses move/rotate/scale/copy through its native object adapter; text replacement retains its separate plain-cell scope; size edits use the published ordinary scalar scope. Complete table observations and the batch use actual serialized-byte budgets. " +
                "replace_dimension_text edits one native aligned/rotated/radial Dimension with automatic text placement, or a manual diametric Dimension already using effective DIMTMOVE=2, with expected_text and plain text up to256 characters. Preserve one <> measurement token, or use empty text for the native value. No persistent dependencies/fields/formatting; diametric text position is preserved and its movement setting is never changed; measured endpoints/style/orientation and the dimension line are retained; DimLinePoint may slide along that same line, automatic text placement may adapt. no other edit family may target that dimension. " +
