ame-part planar face and its lying straight edge, with native radians. Read actual source_relationship, physical plane and unsigned dihedral before native Mirror reuse; no WCS handedness, fixed-coordinate substitution or internal solver is implied. set_model_datum_plane revises a retained fixed native plane with its actual same-part sketch/profile/feature or Mirror consumers. Read datum_plane_revision_ids; supply current datum/revision tokens, last_item_id and every direct_consumer_ids entry through expected_direct_consumer_ids. Legacy expected_mirror_ids remains for Mirror-only scope. Refresh current body_ref after native rebuild and review the intended part and linked drawings. In-plane frame axes are observed representation; projected sketch/dependent-datum/foreign-part adapters are separate; this datum editor does not solve internal sketch controls; use their owning routes. Recovery and Undo are not guaranteed. Read datum_plane_ids for its actual physical plane/host/body membership and fresh token. add_model_mirror accepts a separate definition.datum_plane_id/expected_datum_token branch with existing same-body source features. This retains the exact native plane and its observed definition/drivers/consumers; fixed construction is not a face constraint and native body acquisition is observed without forcing ownership. Refresh returned body_ref and the related model/drawings; recovery and Undo are not guaranteed. create_model_sketch retains committed source_handles projections with exactly one raw plane for standalone construction or support for a same-part planar face or retained healthy WorkPlane in the actual owning document, including compatible document construction without forced body membership. Read inspect_solid_topology(include_native_model_faces=true) for model_face_id/face_token, or inspect_model_history datum_plane_ids for plane_id/datum_token. Owned native_geometry with initial_constraints can accompany retained drawing source_handles or same-part reference_ids in create_model_sketch. Read actual native_inputs member IDs/binding_token for mixed projected/internal relations through add_sketch_constraints; projection operands remain reference-only and service relations are retained. Existing dimensional controls use fresh sketch_constraint_parameter_ids parameter tokens. A stored scalar or VarId alone is not proof that the intended geometry follows a driver; assess meaningful changes with the part and its actual dependent features. Supported source drawing constraints and native feature parameter routes remain separate. create_model_profile retains an unused same-document native sketch/profile with real coplanar source projections and reports actual profile_ownership. set_model_extrusion_profile replaces one existing extrusion contour using a fresh exact profile in the part's actual native owner document, retaining its feature, dimensions/formulas and supported downstream consumers. The replacement parent must already be in the selected part's actual composition, or the profile must have an actual same-part forming consumer. Unused outside document sketches are refused before this rebind setter; profile creation and supported add-from-profile forming retain their separate scope. Read current feature/profile/last IDs and new profile/parent/token; the oriented frame/support remains fixed. Previous construction is preserved with observed ownership, without a release/reuse promise. set_model_profile_regions selects bounded native Circle regions in an existing consumed extrusion profile with fresh profile_region_ids region_token and exact feature/profile/sketch/last IDs. Optional add_source_handles adds real projections of committed coplanar Circle sources to that retained sketch. Separated/nested whole circles support annular holes and multiple nonadjacent regions. region_points are distinct interior WCS points, not boundary indices. Existing sketch/profile/feature identities, original sources, dimensions/formulas and supported later operations remain. Intersecting/tangent circles, adjacent cells requiring union, shared sketches and unrelated geometry need other adapters; no element deletion or internal solver is implied. Recovery and Undo are not guaranteed. set_model_extrusion_extent also has a fresh extrusion_extent_ids branch for native different/symmetric distance modes in an existing part, retaining the exact feature/profile/parent and native downstream consumers. Different uses separate positive-normal native_distance and negative-normal native_distance2 with taper angles in radians. Symmetric retains one native length/taper driver; native_distance is the SDK Distance property, without an assumed total/half physical-thickness conversion. Read actual body WCS bounds and assess the engineering shape. Unchanged expressions and native formula cascades remain; explicitly replacing a changed formula requires replace_driver_formulas=true. Secondary driver IDs may remain null/property-only until native activation; inspect actual result IDs instead of inventing variables. Recovery and Undo are not guaranteed. add_model_extrusion_from_profile, add_model_sweep_from_profile and add_model_revolution_from_profile append native features from one exact retained selected area, including its native Line/Arc/Circle/Spline/Ellipse boundary and holes. add_model_loft_from_profiles consumes two or more ordered existing profile selections with their actual parent sketches and current tokens. Actual forward consumers and nonnull host affinity must match the selected part. Revolution uses a committed coplanar Line axis_handle and positive angle_degrees up to360. Read current profile_ids metadata, parent/profile IDs, selected contour/plane, profile_token and body last_item_id. Native consumption verifies actual body composition and forming ownership. No foreign-body construction transfer or replacement profile is implied; these operations have no guaranteed rollback/Undo. " +
                "Requires explicit bridge/document/expected_revision and unique operation_id shared with create_entities. Rollback is operation-specific; inspect any unknown outcome before further writes. " +
                "After a lost response repeat EXACTLY the same operation_id and payload. Replay is historical, even after Undo; no save or arbitrary commands. For existing coplanar native Regions, boolean_region performs in-place union/intersection/subtract; retain committed read-only tools, use current native plane data and a sole operation. Native Table insert/delete rows/columns retain numeric/formula schedules and existing formats/merges. Reacquire the complete table_token. Structural A1 references, including $ anchors, follow retained cells; interior insertion expands aggregate ranges and partial deletion contracts them. A removed individual reference or whole range requires formula_replacements at BEFORE-operation formula anchors using AFTER-operation coordinates, before any write. New values are an explicit String/Unitless matrix; use native scalar/formula edits for added numeric/formula cells. The kernel evaluates; observed cache/display text may change or be unavailable. Legacy Table RowType datatype/unit getters are explicitly unavailable; actual per-cell types/units/values/formulas and other observed defaults remain checked. Native table lifecycle uses insert_table_rows/delete_table_rows, insert_table_columns/delete_table_columns, merge_table_cells/unmerge_table_cells, set_table_cell_text and set_table_cell_format. Read geometry.editing for the exact current table_token; cell format.appearance_id resolves through response-local appearance_formats for native fill/margins/grids. set_table_cell_format supports true color, background and explicit grid appearance; one lifecycle edit per request and refresh after it. Literal merged-title text edits select its top-left anchor. External/non-formula Fields, links and multiple contents require their owning content adapters; actual same-table formula Fields retain their local bindings/ownership/readable definitions, with private child data explicitly unobserved; same-table A1 arithmetic or native SUM/AVERAGE/COUNT with individual cells and rectangles uses set_table_cell_formula with a fresh table_token. Optional leading = is normalized to one native formula marker; stored HasFormula/expression/reference meaning remain checked. fill_table_formula_range fills a destination rectangle using its top-left expression with explicit relative_references and $ row/column anchors; declared Double result units are not converted. Preserve stored formulas separately from observed evaluated values. Independent exact Table/MLeader/nine Dimension types/non-associative Hatch/Region/Helix support native move/rotate/positive uniform scale/copy in Model or active Paper; copies return native root provenance. Do not transform associated sources through this independent route. Content editors and placement have separate target scopes. Native annotation placement/copies and table lifecycle have no guaranteed rollback/Undo; inspect an unknown outcome.",
